# The edge of the spatial domain: every length at its 1e18 limit or near it.
# Corner to corner the squared distance is 3e36 and the largest squared radius
# 1e36, both below FLT_MAX, so the claim that the limit keeps every structure
# away from overflow is tested here and not only asserted. Teleports and wraps
# across the whole world, k-nearest with k = 300 among 700, rewinds.
